    "locale": "en",
    "title": "Mood check-in: what it is",
    "body": "Around day 14 you will see a short set of mood questions. They are a standard set your care team uses. They are not a diagnosis. You choose who sees the answers, and you can skip them. A clinician reads the answers. The screen you see after answering says by when, and whom to call if you have not heard from us.",
