    "locale": "en",
    "title": "Pelvic floor recovery",
    "body": "The muscles that support your bladder and bowel take time to recover after birth. Leaking urine, pain, or pressure are common and worth raising. Your clinician can talk with you about exercises or a referral to pelvic floor therapy. Ask at your six-week visit or sooner.",
